  "id": "line_up",
  "name": "The Line-Up",
  "description": "The real Line-Up drill racks all 15 reds through the centre of the table, interleaved with the colours on their spots, then pots red-colour-red-colour down the line while building position for the next ball. This trainer only has one object ball and no positional play, so this is a reduced stand-in: all 15 real red positions plus all 6 colours on their real spots, worked in order from the black end down to the brown end -- 21 stops total. The 2 reds below black and 2 between blue and brown are packed one ball-diameter apart against their nearer colour spot (no second spot to space toward there); the 4 between black/pink and 7 between pink/blue are spread roughly evenly across the full real gap between their two colour spots, snapped to the nearest grid row. Grid: rows step 0.0525m (one ball diameter, so black is ~9.5mm off its true spot -- the one real compromise of a uniform grid; pink/baulk are within 3mm; blue and every red are exact), cols step 0.146m (exact for green/center/yellow) -- see assets/puzzles/grid.json. Cue ball is left wide open each time since there's no real position play to place it precisely.",
